    "attributes": {
      "historicalContext": "Catppuccin began in 2021 as a community-driven pastel theme for code editors and terminals, and has since grown into one of the most widely ported color schemes in open source. This adaptation pairs the Latte flavor for light mode with Mocha for dark mode, as packaged by tweakcn.",
      "colorPalette": "Soothing pastels on soft neutral grounds. Light mode (Latte): warm off-white base `#eff1f5` with muted ink text `#4c4f69`; dark mode (Mocha): deep indigo base `#181825` with lavender-tinted text `#cdd6f4`. Mauve (`#8839ef` / `#cba6f7`) leads as primary, Sky (`#04a5e5` / `#89dceb`) accents, Red (`#d20f39` / `#f38ba8`) signals destructive actions. Charts draw from the wider flavor palette: mauve, sky, green, peach, rosewater.",
